      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249141/assets/3d0b6b63883b58ecce92e395380b140b32946a4bb037e1829544539749412af9.png)\n\nLiz deconstructs a lantern and gets the net shown above. In the figure, the areas of two of its faces are shown. What is the total surface area of the lantern?",
      "worked_solution": "The net shown corresponds to a triangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ triangle (base) and $3$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 5+3\\times 13 \\\\  & =5+39 \\\\  & =44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
